      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Graded written paper required — from an English, social studies or history course in the last three years of secondary school","Princeton-specific Questions required","Alumni interview: optional, subject to alumni availability; opting out is not a disadvantage","Arts Supplement: optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/graded-written-paper","label":"Princeton: Graded Written Paper"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/application-checklist","label":"Princeton: First-Year Application Checklist"},{"url":"https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/application-checklist","label":"Princeton: First-Year Application Checklist"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We ask all students to submit a graded written paper for consideration as part of their application to Princeton. … The paper should be from an academic course in English, social studies or history, from the last three years of secondary school, including senior year.","Princeton-specific Questions. In addition to the questions provided by the Common Application, all applicants must submit the Princeton-specific Questions. … Graded Written Paper. A graded written paper is required, preferably in the subjects of English or history.","Interview. Princeton offers optional alumni interviews. … Arts Supplement, if applicable. If you've excelled in architecture, creative writing, dance, music, music theater, theater or visual arts, and would like us to consider your talent, you are welcome to submit an optional Arts Supplement."]}
