    "us-cs-duke": {
      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["Test-optional for first-year and transfer applicants in the 2026–27 cycle, including international students","SAT/ACT scores are considered if submitted; self-reported scores are accepted"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"},{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/resources/","label":"Duke: Resources + FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Duke University is test-optional for both first-year and transfer applicants in the 2026-2027 admissions cycle.","In the 2026-2027 cycle, we will be test-optional for Early and Regular Decision applicants, including international students and students who wish to be considered for our merit scholarships."]},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["English proficiency test recommended, not required, for non-native English speakers or students not in an English-medium curriculum","Minimum scores Duke expects if a test is taken: TOEFL iBT 100 (paper-delivered 75), IELTS 7, Duolingo 130, PTE Academic 70, Cambridge C1 Advanced/C2 Proficiency 180"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you are a non-native English speaker or if you are not currently studying in an English-medium curriculum, we recommend but do not require that you take an English proficiency test. … Cambridge C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency (Minimum score expected is 180) Duolingo (Minimum score expected is 130) IELTS (Minimum band score expected is 7) PTE Academic (Minimum score expected is 70) TOEFL (including the TOEFL Home Edition) Minimum scores expected: 100 on the internet-based TOEFL","note":"Duke states these as minimum expected scores for a recommended (not required) test; no preference among tests, highest score used."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Application for Regular Decision High School Transcript Secondary School Report with Counselor Recommendation Two Teacher Recommendations SAT and/or ACT Scores (optional","note":"Duke’s 2026–27 first-year checklist lists transcript, school report, recommendations and optional SAT/ACT; no course-specific admissions test."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"We recommend four years of English and at least three years of mathematics, natural sciences, world language, and social studies. We generally expect students to enroll in five academic courses per year, and if a student does not take four years in a particular subject area, it should be replaced with an academic course of equal rigor. For students applying to the Pratt School of Engineering, we require coursework in calculus and strongly recommend physics.","note":"Official: Duke recommends four years of English and at least three years of mathematics, natural sciences, world language and social studies (recommended, not required). The Pratt-only calculus requirement does not apply: this course is in Trinity College of Arts & Sciences.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists recommended high-school coursework (4 years English; at least 3 years each of mathematics, natural sciences, world language, social studies); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"A-level and similar national exam results are considered from students who choose to submit them (optional; self-reported results accepted for review).","sources":[{"url":"https://undergraduate.bulletins.duke.edu/policies-procedures/admissions","label":"Duke: 2026–27 Undergraduate Instruction Bulletin — C.6. Admissions"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Duke University will continue to consider self-reported and/or official scores from the SAT and ACT, English proficiency tests, Advanced Placement tests, International Baccalaureate exams, and A-level and other similar national exams from students who choose to submit them.","note":"Stated in the 2026–27 Undergraduate Instruction Bulletin; Duke’s admissions pages mention A-levels only for placement credit after enrolling."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"IB scores are optional: considered if reported, and Duke asks students to self-report them in the application.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"},{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/resources/","label":"Duke: Resources + FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We will consider other scores like AP and IB scores, if you choose to report them.","We value those scores when available as demonstrations of subject mastery to complement your academic transcripts. You should self-report these scores in your application."]},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP scores are optional — considered if reported and self-reported in the application"],"note":"AP/IB course credit and placement are granted only after admission (Registrar’s Office) and are not admission requirements, so they are not recorded here.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"},{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/resources/","label":"Duke: Resources + FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["We will consider other scores like AP and IB scores, if you choose to report them.","We value those scores when available as demonstrations of subject mastery to complement your academic transcripts. You should self-report these scores in your application."]},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Apply to Trinity College of Arts & Sciences (this course) or the Pratt School of Engineering","Two required Duke short essays (250 words each) in 2026–27; further short essays optional","Alumni interviews: optional, not offered to all applicants","Arts supplement: optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.duke.edu/apply/","label":"Duke: Apply"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Trinity College of Arts & Sciences or Pratt School of Engineering? … The following questions are required for all first-year applicants to Duke University during the 2026-27 application cycle. (250 word limit) … Alumni interviews are an optional component of the Duke application process. … If you intend to continue your arts activity at Duke, you may submit one (1) optional arts supplement to be evaluated by a Duke University faculty member in that program or department."}
    },
