      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/high-school-courses/index.html","label":"Northwestern: High School Courses FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"The Weinberg College of Arts and Sciences, the Medill School of Journalism, the School of Education and Social Policy, the Bienen School of Music and the School of Communication require that entering students complete a minimum of 16 courses (most applicants present more) in the following academic areas:","note":"Official: Weinberg College of Arts and Sciences requires entering students to complete a minimum of 16 courses: English 4 full-year courses; one foreign language at least 2 full-year courses; history and social science at least 2; laboratory science at least 2; mathematics at least 3; plus 1–3 additional full-year courses in those areas.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists required high-school coursework for Weinberg (minimum 16 courses incl. English 4, maths 3, foreign language 2, lab science 2, history/social science 2); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
