      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Northwestern writing supplement required (one 300-word question; up to two optional short questions encouraged)","Applicants apply to one of Northwestern’s undergraduate schools; the same review criteria apply to all","No alumni interviews; InitialView interviews accepted (optional) from students at international high schools","Optional: Mathematical Methods in the Social Sciences (MMSS) has a separate application; a year of calculus is required for MMSS admission"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/requirements.html","label":"Northwestern: Application Materials"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/advice/academic-path.html","label":"Northwestern: Your Academic Path"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/requirements.html","label":"Northwestern: Application Materials"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/requirements.html","label":"Northwestern: Application Materials"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["The following question is required for all Common Application and Coalition with Scoir applicants (optional for QuestBridge applicants). Please respond in 300 words or fewer:","Northwestern requires all applicants to apply to one of the six undergraduate schools. There is no strategic advantage to applying to any specific school, as we use the same admission review criteria for all Northwestern undergraduate applicants.","Northwestern no longer offers alumni interviews as an optional part of the application process. … For students applying from international high schools, Northwestern accepts interviews from InitialView. Similar to Glimpse videos, InitialView interviews are not required and applicants without one are at no disadvantage in our review process.","The application processes to Northwestern and to MMSS are separate. Admission to Northwestern is not a guarantee of admission to the MMSS and the status of your MMSS application will not affect your Northwestern general acceptance decision. … A strong high school curriculum, including a year of calculus, is required for admission."]}
