      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["SAT or ACT required for first-year applicants to all Cornell undergraduate colleges and schools (from fall 2026 entry onward)","Scores may be self-reported; ACT science section not required"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.cornell.edu/policies/standardized-testing-policy","label":"Cornell: Standardized Testing Policy"},{"url":"https://faq.enrollment.cornell.edu/kb/article/1-does-cornell-university-require-the-sat-or-act/","label":"Cornell Admissions FAQ: Does Cornell require the SAT or ACT?"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["First-year applicants are required to submit SAT or ACT scores when applying to Cornell.","Effective for students applying to enroll for fall 2026 or beyond, applicants to all Cornell undergraduate colleges and schools will be required to submit standardized test scores."]},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["English proficiency exam required unless you are a U.S. citizen/permanent resident, English is your native language, or English has been your primary language of instruction for the past four years","Accepted: TOEFL, IELTS, Duolingo English Test, Cambridge C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.cornell.edu/policies/standardized-testing-policy","label":"Cornell: Standardized Testing Policy"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"English has been the primary language of instruction for the past four years. … Applicants who do not meet one of these criteria are required to submit an English proficiency exam score. Accepted exams and score requirements to be most competitive in our admissions review process include: … TOEFL exams taken prior to January 2026: minimum score of 100 … TOEFL exams taken January 2026 or later: minimum score of 5.0, recommended score of 5.5 … IELTS, minimum score of 7.5 … Duolingo English Test, minimum score of 130 … Cambridge C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency, minimum score of 191","note":"Cornell lists scores as “score requirements to be most competitive in our admissions review process” — a description of competitive applicants, so no score is shown as a requirement. Self-reported scores accepted; enrolling students must send official scores."},
